Changelog
Device: Xiaomi Mi 11 Lite 5G (renoir)
Date: 26/09/2026
* Kernel & Root
  * Integrated ReSukiSU v4.2.0 (in-tree driver, version code 40796, UAPI v4).
  * Integrated SuSFS 5.4 (v2.3.0) with inline hooks for suspicious path/mount hiding, kstat spoofing, and open redirection.
  * Switched zram compression from LZO to Huawei LZ4KD for improved memory compression performance.

Date: 25/09/2026
* Initial LineageOS 24.0 (Android 17) Bringup
  * Brought up device, vendor-common, and camera trees for Android 17 (Cinnamon Bun).
* GApps
  * Bundled MindTheGapps inline for Android 17 (Google Play Store, Play Services, GSF, Setup Wizard, Restore).
* MIUI Camera
  * Fixed front camera video recording crash (resolved EIS buffer import mismatch and enforced format override).
  * Added public libraries whitelist for Xiaomi camera algorithm libraries.
  * Updated camera compatibility shims (libgui_shim_miuicamera, BnProducerListener) for Android 17.
* Dolby Stack
  * Rebuilt Dolby Codec2 service (vendor.dolby.media.c2@1.0-service) natively from source to resolve Android 17 ABI crash.
  * Restored full Dolby Atmos & Dolby Vision media playback without mediaserver aborts.
* SystemUI & Status Bar
  * Defaulted cellular data icon to 4G instead of LTE.
  * Added status bar NFC icon with toggle support in settings.
* Wi-Fi Display (WFD)
  * Updated WFD proprietary blobs to modern marvel_g baseline with V2 AIDL session support.
  * Added WfdCommon compatibility patch for modern Android.
* Sepolicy & Stability
  * Cleaned up duplicate touch and powershare SELinux definitions.
  * Fixed vibrator Soong config boolean types.

Date: 14/06/2026
Kernel
* Fix unexpected reboot after system shutdown
Resolved an issue where the device would
automatically initiate a reboot sequence immediately
after a successful shutdown. This ensures the device
remains powered off as intended.
* Upgraded Dolby Vision Stack: Switched to a newer
  standalone Dolby Vision stack backported from
   Android 16. credits to @swiitchOFF for the commits 

Date: 09/06/2026
* **Source Architecture Overhaul**
  * Fully rebased and updated the device, device/vendor-common, and vendor tree structures for improved build stability.
* **Audio Stack Enhancements**
  * Upgraded the Dolby Atmos subsystem to a newer version, optimizing audio processing and sound stage profiles.
  * Integrated native support for **E-AC3** (Dolby Digital Plus) audio decoding.
* **Display & Media Engine**
  * Restored native **Dolby Vision** support, fully optimized for compatibility with the Android 16 framework.

